  "body": "During discussion in Mozilla London All-hands, it seems clear the term \"site\" has caused confusing during verbal discussion; we had to put `site: eTLD+1, e.g. example.co.uk` on the whiteboard and say \"the site per spec\" to avoid confusion (to the normal concept of site as used in daily life and on UI label).\n\nWould it be easier to use a more obscure term like \"origin group\" so there can be a distinctive definition? The related terms like \"site storage\" or \"site storage unit\" would need to be revised as well.\n",
